  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting vocational training for youth, including internally displaced persons</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to rehabilitate and reactivate six Technical and Vocational Training Centres (TVTCs) in Aden, Lahj, and Ta&apos;iz. This intervention will focus on infrastructure rehabilitation, including classrooms, workshops, and gender-segregated WASH facilities. Additional efforts will include equipping training centres with tools and appliances, improving accessibility for people with disabilities, and installing solar power systems for sustainable electricity. The project will promote sustainable, gender-inclusive livelihoods by providing vocational training and technical skills development to conflict-affected populations. A market-based approach will enhance employment opportunities, particularly for women, fostering inclusive workforce participation. By empowering individuals with practical skills and supporting small businesses, this initiative aims to improve resilience, economic stability, and long-term social development in Yemen&apos;s most vulnerable communities. Lastly, the project will ensure the sustainability of the targeted TVTCs by conducting capacity-building trainings for TVTC teaching staff. This will allow to ensure that the teaching staff is supported through the improved infrastructure of TVTCs and capacity-building initiatives, empowering them to deliver lessons that are effective and engaging, and make the most of the school facilities.</narrative>
  </description>
